Re: SCP Looking for greenlight


17 Nov 2020 18:50






Hey! Not a greelighter, sorry.

So, I'm a fan of your base concept. A warehouse that changes environment every night could make for some very interesting exploration logs and pave way for diverse experiences. I do have to wonder, however, how exactly the changes that occur in the warehouse relate to the qualities you listed? This would be good to know, as it would give the SCP a little more structure as opposed to being entirely random or too specific in its activation conditions.

One concern I have about the object is that it seems like any exploration made into the warehouse during its activation period seems to be a death sentence (excluding times when the inside changes to a paradisiacal environment), so why would the Foundation continue to send in exploration teams? They don't often simply throw away D-Class and MTF members in order to study this type of thing. Try to create a reason for them to explore it- some reward they could gain, or some unfortunate event if it is not explored. This way, we have some motive for the Foundation's actions, which is important.

Overall, I don't think there's all too much that needs to be done to this concept; at its core, it's already interesting and will give the reader a nice series of anecdotes to read. Good luck developing the concept further, if need be, and I hope to see this one fully fleshed out!







